    {
      "value": "<p>Commissioned to record a tether of local construction and local design, and to establish, in the Consortium&#39;s own wording, on whose initiative the assistance had been offered. It produced a complete metric survey of the anchor works, four hundred hours of interview, and the eleven hundred pages of the suspension file that concern who asked for the tether and in what words. Contact was suspended in 2298 while the inquiry was still in the field. It is the second most expensive entry here and the one whose findings are most often described, by people who have read them, as inconclusive.</p>",
